Subject: [PATCH] mtd: gpmi: refuse NAND writes for read-only qualification

Partitions are read-only as well. Guard controller commands so even BBT
maintenance during probe cannot program or erase the original NAND.
Only the explicit diagnostic DT property enables this guard.

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/gpmi-nand/gpmi-nand.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/gpmi-nand/gpmi-nand.c
@@ -2515,6 +2515,23 @@
 	if (check_only)
 		return 0;
 
+	if (of_property_read_bool(this->dev->of_node, "galdrun,read-only")) {
+		for (i = 0; i < op->ninstrs; i++) {
+			if (op->instrs[i].type != NAND_OP_CMD_INSTR)
+				continue;
+			switch (op->instrs[i].ctx.cmd.opcode) {
+			case NAND_CMD_SEQIN:
+			case NAND_CMD_RNDIN:
+			case NAND_CMD_PAGEPROG:
+			case NAND_CMD_CACHEDPROG:
+			case NAND_CMD_ERASE1:
+			case NAND_CMD_ERASE2:
+				dev_err(this->dev, "NAND write refused: read-only qualification\n");
+				return -EROFS;
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
 	this->ntransfers = 0;
 	for (i = 0; i < GPMI_MAX_TRANSFERS; i++)
 		this->transfers[i].direction = DMA_NONE;
